cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GlassNN in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
title: "GlassNN: a transparent teaching library for neural networks"
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-19"
abstract: >-
  GlassNN is a small neural-network library for teaching, written to be
  read. It implements reverse-mode automatic differentiation, layers from
  multilayer perceptrons to the transformer encoder, and the usual
  optimizers in NumPy, with PyTorch's names and defaults, an optional CuPy
  backend for NVIDIA GPUs, and a book that derives every operation next to
  its code.
keywords:
  - neural networks
  - automatic differentiation
  - deep learning
  - teaching
  - NumPy
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bioinfo-recetox/glassnn"
url: "https://bioinfo-recetox.github.io/glassnn/"
authors:
  - family-names: Popovici
    given-names: Vlad
    affiliation: "RECETOX - Faculty of Science, Masaryk University"
